>>
Rule 2 (broadcasting when ranks are equal: per-dimension equal or 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (when v_1 has extra leading dims, they must be size 1 for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > ndim(v_2) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1
>>
Rule 4 (when v_2 has extra leading dims, they must be size 1 for broadcasting)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) > ndim(v_1) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 6 (negative exponents require bases to be nonzero everywhere)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if max(v_2) < 0 then min(v_1) > 0 ∨ max(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 7 (single-dimension right-aligned broadcasting for v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = 1 then shape(v_2, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 1
